2026-11-19 04:47:06 - Agent_20261119044255 - INFO - [+] Agent signaled completion: Reviewed the lxml group covering 4 queries (17 raw results) across build/setup scripts and library code.

Key outcomes:

TRUE POSITIVES:
1. src/lxml/ElementInclude.py:118 (_lxml_default_loader) — the XInclude default loader performs urlopen(href) on any href containing "://", and href originates from untrusted document content via urljoin(base_url, e.get("href")) in _include(). Any app calling ElementInclude.include() on attacker-supplied XML gets arbitrary URL fetch (SSRF) and local file disclosure. There is a max_depth recursion guard but no network/scheme restriction. TP, medium.
2. src/lxml/html/html5parser.py:230 (parse) — html5parser.parse() calls urlopen(filename_url_or_file) whenever the argument "looks like a URL" (any non-empty scheme), so a user-controlled string is fetched server-side with no scheme/host allowlist. Network access is on by default for the URL branch. TP, medium.

MANUAL REVIEW:
3. src/lxml/html/__init__.py:1136-1141 (FormElement.submit / open_http_urllib) — form.action comes from parsed (potentially attacker-controlled) HTML and is passed straight to urlopen; documented "FIXME: should test that it's not a relative URL or something". By-design browser-like behavior but a real SSRF sink when lxml.html is used to process untrusted pages.
4. src/lxml/html/html5parser.py:228 — same URL-detection helper (_looks_like_url) that gates the fetch; MR as the decision point for #2.
5. buildlibxml.py:318 (call_subprocess in cmmi) — subprocess.call with a non-constant cmd list; arguments come from static build configuration (configure args, --with-* flags) and env defaults, not from remote input. Development/build-time only, no shell=True, so MR/low.

FALSE POSITIVES:
- buildlibxml.py:64/149/159/173/294 — downloader plumbing for libxml2/libxslt source tarballs from hard-coded release URLs during a developer-initiated build; urlretrieve with fixed destinations, no attacker-controlled input.
- setupinfo.py:355 run_command — shell=True but commands are built from hard-coded program names (pkg-config/xml2-config/xslt-config/xcrun) and constant option strings; run at build time only.
- setupinfo.py:361-362 Popen(shell=True) — the only variable parts are developer-controlled build options, so no injection vector from untrusted input.

